    {
      "id": "claim_7141bd4e22104694a87f38509a37d508",
      "statement": "The GET /v1/search endpoint (search_coffee_beans) is the backend that powers faceted filtering. It accepts all filter parameters as FastAPI Query parameters (including list[str] for multi-select filters like roaster, roaster_location, origin), validates sort_by against a Literal of allowed values, validates currency codes, constructs a FilterParams, and returns APIResponse[list[APISearchResult]] with PaginationInfo and metadata containing max_possible_score.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/kissaten/api/main.py#L1855-L1957",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9b82800e12913c2c790498c56b5cecbd46edbf92b7f42e87a01de461bd4d1bad:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/kissaten/schemas/api_models.py#L94-L108",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dfdfbb2217e539b1e0c9ec7064b44fda33e12d8763a86ff783db382675482cc4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d0c70060b7fa43f6bc272be3128e3937",
      "statement": "build_coffee_bean_filters() compiles FilterParams into a FilterResult containing: conditions (AND-joined WHERE clauses for strict mode), params, score_components (CASE WHEN ... THEN weight ELSE 0 END expressions for relevance mode), hard_conditions/hard_params (always-applied WHERE filters). It handles each filter type differently: roaster uses IN, origin uses EXISTS subqueries on the origins table, region/producer/farm use normalised matching with ILIKE fallback for complex boolean queries, process checks both o.process and o.process_common_name, variety checks both o.variety and unnested o.variety_canonical array elements, and elevation uses MAX(o.elevation_max) across all origins for the bean.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/kissaten/api/main.py#L206-L604",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:eb98811d1f7772c7f1b6f856cf3af0e88160ef8d45f56747e5cc981a56902e97:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5146836050ee408da2420aaacab155be",
      "statement": "Some filters are always applied as hard WHERE conditions regardless of sort mode because showing beans that violate them would be misleading: in_stock_only (cb.in_stock = true), is_decaf (cb.is_decaf = ?), is_tasting_kit (cb.is_tasting_kit = ?), and the default requires_review hide clause (cb.requires_review = false for public search, overridable only by admin include_unreviewed). In contrast, is_single_origin is a soft score component in relevance mode but a hard WHERE filter in strict mode.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/kissaten/api/main.py#L580-L603",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:65bfe9708f5a638c3382d282452761ae8a4eb3da812cae8174ae9982c61ce132:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_026c823100d64947b7130e11dae54d44",
      "statement": "The /v1/search endpoint has two modes. In relevance mode (sort_by=relevance), build_coffee_bean_filters is called with use_scoring=True, producing score components; results are filtered with WHERE score > 0 (any matching filter suffices) and ordered by score DESC, name ASC, sb.id ASC, with max_possible_score (the count of score components) returned in metadata for frontend partitioning into 'matching' and 'similar' buckets. In strict mode (any other sort), build_coffee_bean_filters is called a second time with use_scoring=False, producing AND-joined WHERE conditions that all filters must satisfy, ordered by the user-selected sort field with sb.id ASC as a deterministic tiebreaker for stable pagination.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/kissaten/api/main.py#L2030-L2092",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fe2589de57721ffebb92ce5d9cfb6fb3ec6f6e298fca4740b07452db63dde223:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a3cc143a0e224e9487e8addb64a34f99",
      "statement": "The price_large sort ('Bulk price') normalises price comparisons across different bag sizes by sorting on the price per kg of the largest available bag. Both the count and main queries define a largest_bag CTE that uses DISTINCT ON (bean_id) with ORDER BY bean_id, weight DESC, price DESC to select the heaviest bag per bean, exposing lb_weight, lb_price, lb_currency, and lb_price_per_kg_usd. The main query LEFT JOINs this CTE, and price_large maps to COALESCE(sb.lb_price_per_kg_usd, sb.price_usd / NULLIF(sb.weight, 0)). The min_large_weight filter (AND cb.lb_weight >= ?) constrains results to beans whose largest bag is at least the specified weight.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/kissaten/api/main.py#L2058-L2070",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b401af44f8775f1608eb968ce6ccbc9e40ed10503d5b91c297416603336f65d0:"
        },
