    {
      "id": "claim_369a630effca4351a8ccf3e8d261e4a0",
      "statement": "The text-based filters support a shared boolean query syntax compiled server-side by parse_boolean_search_query_for_field(): | for OR, & for AND, ! or NOT for negation, * and ? for wildcards, () for grouping, and quoted strings for case-insensitive exact matches. The SearchFilters component surfaces this syntax with inline help text. Terms are compiled into DuckDB ILIKE predicates (or = for exact matches) with strip_accents() applied when the field has a pre-computed unaccented variant.",
      "evidence": [
