      "id": "claim_3f698a11a869429b9728c2e0d036e9b5",
      "statement": "Invalid filter values that cause a 400 API response are caught by +page.ts and returned as searchError data (not thrown) so the page renders with an error message and the filter form remains usable. The searchStore.performNewSearch catches network errors and sets the store error field, clearing results; loadMore catches errors but preserves existing results so the user does not lose scroll position.",
